{"id":"chatcmpl-22c76935-8894-45d5-87cf-20ac6c30d8d8","object":"chat.completion","created":1795249962,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a laterality-sensitive medical image question by combining an expert-model query with a grounded, coordinate-based report to independently confirm the finding. The key strategy is to explicitly ask about directionality (left vs. right) and cross-validate across two independent evidence sources before committing to an answer. Success hinges on verifying patient laterality rather than relying on a single model's output.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question hinges on left/right or directional distinctions, explicitly query the model for the direction of the finding rather than asking a generic 'what is present' question.\",\n    \"Use two independent evidence sources (e.g., an expert model and a grounded/coordinate-based report) and require agreement before finalizing a laterality-sensitive answer.\",\n    \"Request grounded reports with spatial coordinates to verify that the described finding matches the correct anatomical side and patient orientation.\",\n    \"Decompose the diagnostic question into a targeted sub-question (e.g., 'which way does the spine curve?') that directly discriminates between the given options.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Ask direction-specific sub-questions and confirm laterality with a second, coordinate-grounded source before answering.\",\n    \"Binary choice with spatial semantics\": \"Convert the option set into a single discriminating question (direction/side) and gather independent confirmation.\",\n    \"Multi-tool verification\": \"Pair a domain-expert model with a structured/grounded reporting tool; treat agreement as the decision criterion.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding's direction/side explicitly matches one of the provided options.\",\n    \"Verify patient laterality (left vs. right) is correctly interpreted before selecting the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":436,"total_tokens":802,"completion_tokens":366,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":436},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":366}}}